js-gh-image-fallback\"></a>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Description</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Text elements inside the pricing wizard modal (step counter \"1/4\", question title, option labels, and the \"Back\" button) are invisible due to matching font and background colors. Text is only readable when highlighted manually.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Acceptance Criteria:</h2>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Update CSS color rules so all text elements (heading, option lists, step indicator, and navigation buttons) are clearly visible against the white modal background.</li>\n<li>Ensure color contrast meets standard accessibility guidelines (WCAG).</li>\n</ol>",
